{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" hook provides a compatibility layer that accepts the v8-style API while using v9 under the hood. This is useful for teams that need to migrate incrementally or have large codebases where a full migration isn't immediately practical."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"warning","title":"Warning","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deprecated"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and intended only as a temporary migration aid. It includes all features by default, so the bundle is larger than with the tree-shakeable v9 API. Plan to migrate to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":" for better performance and smaller bundles."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-uselegacytable","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have an existing v8 codebase and need to upgrade dependencies"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want to migrate incrementally, one table at a time"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You need v9 compatibility but don't have time for a full migration yet"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from 'react'\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  legacyCreateColumnHelper,\n  useLegacyTable,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\nimport type {\n  ColumnFiltersState,\n  PaginationState,\n  SortingState,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport type {\n  LegacyColumn,\n  LegacyColumnDef,\n  LegacyRow,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n\ninterface Person {\n  name: string\n  email: string\n  age: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = legacyCreateColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns: LegacyColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', { header: 'Name' }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('email', { header: 'Email' }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', { header: 'Age' }),\n  columnHelper.display({ id: 'actions', header: 'Actions' }),\n]\n\nfunction MyTable({ data }: { data: Person[] }) {\n  const [sorting, setSorting] = useState<SortingState>([])\n  const [columnFilters, setColumnFilters] = useState<ColumnFiltersState>([])\n  const [pagination, setPagination] = useState<PaginationState>({\n    pageIndex: 0,\n    pageSize: 10,\n  })\n\n  // useLegacyTable accepts the v8-style API\n  const table = useLegacyTable({\n    columns,\n    data,\n    getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n    getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n    getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n    getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n    state: { sorting, columnFilters, pagination },\n    onSortingChange: setSorting,\n    onColumnFiltersChange: setColumnFilters,\n    onPaginationChange: setPagination,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <table>\n      <thead>\n        {table.getHeaderGroups().map((headerGroup) => (\n          <tr key={headerGroup.id}>\n            {headerGroup.headers.map((header) => (\n              <th key={header.id}>\n                {flexRender(\n                  header.column.columnDef.header,\n                  header.getContext(),\n                )}\n                {header.column.getCanFilter() ? (\n                  <Filter column={header.column} />\n                ) : null}\n              </th>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        {table.getRowModel().rows.map((row) => (\n          <tr key={row.id}>\n            {row.getAllCells().map((cell) => (\n              <td key={cell.id}>\n                {cell.column.id === 'actions' ? (\n                  <RowActions row={row} />\n                ) : (\n                  flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n                )}\n              </td>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction Filter({ column }: { column: LegacyColumn<Person> }) {\n  return (\n    <input\n      value={(column.getFilterValue() as string) ?? ''}\n      onChange={(e) => column.setFilterValue(e.target.value)}\n      placeholder=\"Filter...\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RowActions({ row }: { row: LegacyRow<Person> }) {\n  return <button onClick={() => console.log(row.original)}>Edit</button>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-helpers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Helpers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":", use these type helpers for proper TypeScript support:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LegacyColumnDef<TData>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definition type (equivalent to v8's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnDef<TData>"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LegacyColumn<TData>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column instance type"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LegacyRow<TData>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row instance type"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LegacyCell<TData>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell instance type"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LegacyTable<TData>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table instance type"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"legacyCreateColumnHelper<TData>()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column helper with StockFeatures pre-bound; only requires TData"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-legacycreatecolumnhelper","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"legacyCreateColumnHelper"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"legacyCreateColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":". It has StockFeatures pre-bound, so you only need to specify "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { legacyCreateColumnHelper } from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\nimport type { LegacyColumnDef } from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n\nconst columnHelper = legacyCreateColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns: LegacyColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', { header: 'Name' }),\n  // ...\n]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-differences-from-v8","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Differences from v8"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" aims for v8 compatibility, there are a few differences:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"row-model-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Model Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get*RowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":" functions are imported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-table/legacy"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getExpandedRowModel,\n  getGroupedRowModel,\n  getFacetedRowModel,\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues,\n  getFacetedUniqueValues,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sorting-function-renames","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting Function Renames"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that in v9, sorting-related APIs have been renamed. If you're using custom sorting functions in column definitions:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The legacy table adapter handles this internally for built-in sorting, but if you're defining custom sorting functions, be aware of the rename."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"caveats-and-limitations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caveats and Limitations"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"bundle-size","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundle Size"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" includes "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"all features"}]},{"type":"text","value":" by default, similar to v8. This means:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No tree-shaking benefits"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundle size is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"much larger"}]},{"type":"text","value":" than v8, since each feature has grown since v8 and you pay for all of them"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tree-shakeable v9 API exists so TanStack Table can add features over time without bloating everyone's bundles; only users who opt into a feature pay for it"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If bundle size is a concern, prioritize migrating to the full v9 API"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"deprecation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" is deprecated and will be removed in a future major version. It exists solely to ease migration. Plan your migration timeline accordingly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"full-state-subscription-only","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full-State Subscription Only"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" always subscribes to the entire table state, so the component that creates the table re-renders on every state change, just like v8. The fine-grained rendering optimizations of v9 (narrow "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":" selectors) are not available through the legacy hook."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"no-createtablehook-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" Integration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be used with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":". If you want to create reusable table configurations, migrate to the full v9 API."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migration-path","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Path"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once you're ready to migrate to the full v9 API:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLegacyTable"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get*RowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":" options to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowModels"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update types from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Legacy*"},{"type":"text","value":" to the standard v9 types"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./migrating.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"main migration guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for complete instructions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-use-legacy-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic useLegacyTable example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a working implementation."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"when-to-use-uselegacytable","text":"When to Use useLegacyTable","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"type-helpers","text":"Type Helpers","level":2},{"id":"using-legacycreatecolumnhelper","text":"Using legacyCreateColumnHelper","level":3},{"id":"api-differences-from-v8","text":"API Differences from v8","level":2},{"id":"row-model-functions","text":"Row Model Functions","level":3},{"id":"sorting-function-renames","text":"Sorting Function Renames","level":3},{"id":"caveats-and-limitations","text":"Caveats and Limitations","level":2},{"id":"bundle-size","text":"Bundle Size","level":3},{"id":"deprecation","text":"Deprecation","level":3},{"id":"full-state-subscription-only","text":"Full-State Subscription Only","level":3},{"id":"no-createtablehook-integration","text":"No createTableHook Integration","level":3},{"id":"migration-path","text":"Migration Path","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `useLegacyTable` hook provides a compatibility layer that accepts the v8-style API while using v9 under the hood. This is useful for teams that need to migrate incrementally or have large codebases where a full migration isn't immediately practical.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> `useLegacyTable` is **deprecated** and intended only as a temporary migration aid. It includes all features by default, so the bundle is larger than with the tree-shakeable v9 API. Plan to migrate to `useTable` for better performance and smaller bundles.\n\n## When to Use `useLegacyTable`\n\n- You have an existing v8 codebase and need to upgrade dependencies\n- You want to migrate incrementally, one table at a time\n- You need v9 compatibility but don't have time for a full migration yet\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  legacyCreateColumnHelper,\n  useLegacyTable,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\nimport type {\n  ColumnFiltersState,\n  PaginationState,\n  SortingState,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport type {\n  LegacyColumn,\n  LegacyColumnDef,\n  LegacyRow,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n\ninterface Person {\n  name: string\n  email: string\n  age: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = legacyCreateColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns: LegacyColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', { header: 'Name' }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('email', { header: 'Email' }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', { header: 'Age' }),\n  columnHelper.display({ id: 'actions', header: 'Actions' }),\n]\n\nfunction MyTable({ data }: { data: Person[] }) {\n  const [sorting, setSorting] = useState<SortingState>([])\n  const [columnFilters, setColumnFilters] = useState<ColumnFiltersState>([])\n  const [pagination, setPagination] = useState<PaginationState>({\n    pageIndex: 0,\n    pageSize: 10,\n  })\n\n  // useLegacyTable accepts the v8-style API\n  const table = useLegacyTable({\n    columns,\n    data,\n    getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n    getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n    getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n    getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n    state: { sorting, columnFilters, pagination },\n    onSortingChange: setSorting,\n    onColumnFiltersChange: setColumnFilters,\n    onPaginationChange: setPagination,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <table>\n      <thead>\n        {table.getHeaderGroups().map((headerGroup) => (\n          <tr key={headerGroup.id}>\n            {headerGroup.headers.map((header) => (\n              <th key={header.id}>\n                {flexRender(\n                  header.column.columnDef.header,\n                  header.getContext(),\n                )}\n                {header.column.getCanFilter() ? (\n                  <Filter column={header.column} />\n                ) : null}\n              </th>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        {table.getRowModel().rows.map((row) => (\n          <tr key={row.id}>\n            {row.getAllCells().map((cell) => (\n              <td key={cell.id}>\n                {cell.column.id === 'actions' ? (\n                  <RowActions row={row} />\n                ) : (\n                  flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n                )}\n              </td>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction Filter({ column }: { column: LegacyColumn<Person> }) {\n  return (\n    <input\n      value={(column.getFilterValue() as string) ?? ''}\n      onChange={(e) => column.setFilterValue(e.target.value)}\n      placeholder=\"Filter...\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RowActions({ row }: { row: LegacyRow<Person> }) {\n  return <button onClick={() => console.log(row.original)}>Edit</button>\n}\n```\n\n## Type Helpers\n\nWhen using `useLegacyTable`, use these type helpers for proper TypeScript support:\n\n| Type                                | Description                                                     |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `LegacyColumnDef<TData>`            | Column definition type (equivalent to v8's `ColumnDef<TData>`)  |\n| `LegacyColumn<TData>`               | Column instance type                                            |\n| `LegacyRow<TData>`                  | Row instance type                                               |\n| `LegacyCell<TData>`                 | Cell instance type                                              |\n| `LegacyTable<TData>`                | Table instance type                                             |\n| `legacyCreateColumnHelper<TData>()` | Column helper with StockFeatures pre-bound; only requires TData |\n\n### Using `legacyCreateColumnHelper`\n\nUse `legacyCreateColumnHelper` instead of `createColumnHelper`. It has StockFeatures pre-bound, so you only need to specify `TData`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { legacyCreateColumnHelper } from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\nimport type { LegacyColumnDef } from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n\nconst columnHelper = legacyCreateColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns: LegacyColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', { header: 'Name' }),\n  // ...\n]\n```\n\n## API Differences from v8\n\nWhile `useLegacyTable` aims for v8 compatibility, there are a few differences:\n\n### Row Model Functions\n\nThe `get*RowModel()` functions are imported from `@tanstack/react-table/legacy`:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getExpandedRowModel,\n  getGroupedRowModel,\n  getFacetedRowModel,\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues,\n  getFacetedUniqueValues,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n```\n\n### Sorting Function Renames\n\nNote that in v9, sorting-related APIs have been renamed. If you're using custom sorting functions in column definitions:\n\n| v8          | v9       |\n| ----------- | -------- |\n| `sortingFn` | `sortFn` |\n\nThe legacy table adapter handles this internally for built-in sorting, but if you're defining custom sorting functions, be aware of the rename.\n\n## Caveats and Limitations\n\n### Bundle Size\n\n`useLegacyTable` includes **all features** by default, similar to v8. This means:\n\n- No tree-shaking benefits\n- Bundle size is **much larger** than v8, since each feature has grown since v8 and you pay for all of them\n- The tree-shakeable v9 API exists so TanStack Table can add features over time without bloating everyone's bundles; only users who opt into a feature pay for it\n- If bundle size is a concern, prioritize migrating to the full v9 API\n\n### Deprecation\n\n`useLegacyTable` is deprecated and will be removed in a future major version. It exists solely to ease migration. Plan your migration timeline accordingly.\n\n### Full-State Subscription Only\n\n`useLegacyTable` always subscribes to the entire table state, so the component that creates the table re-renders on every state change, just like v8. The fine-grained rendering optimizations of v9 (narrow `useTable` selectors) are not available through the legacy hook.\n\n### No `createTableHook` Integration\n\n`useLegacyTable` cannot be used with `createTableHook`. If you want to create reusable table configurations, migrate to the full v9 API.\n\n## Migration Path\n\nOnce you're ready to migrate to the full v9 API:\n\n1. Replace `useLegacyTable` with `useTable`\n2. Define your `features` using `tableFeatures()`\n3. Convert `get*RowModel()` options to `rowModels`\n4. Update types from `Legacy*` to the standard v9 types\n\nSee the [main migration guide](./migrating.md) for complete instructions.\n\n## Example\n\nSee the [Basic useLegacyTable example](../examples/basic-use-legacy-table) for a working implementation.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Using useLegacyTable for Incremental Migration\n---\n\nThe `useLegacyTable` hook provides a compatibility layer that accepts the v8-style API while using v9 under the hood. This is useful for teams that need to migrate incrementally or have large codebases where a full migration isn't immediately practical.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> `useLegacyTable` is **deprecated** and intended only as a temporary migration aid. It includes all features by default, so the bundle is larger than with the tree-shakeable v9 API. Plan to migrate to `useTable` for better performance and smaller bundles.\n\n## When to Use `useLegacyTable`\n\n- You have an existing v8 codebase and need to upgrade dependencies\n- You want to migrate incrementally, one table at a time\n- You need v9 compatibility but don't have time for a full migration yet\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  legacyCreateColumnHelper,\n  useLegacyTable,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\nimport type {\n  ColumnFiltersState,\n  PaginationState,\n  SortingState,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport type {\n  LegacyColumn,\n  LegacyColumnDef,\n  LegacyRow,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n\ninterface Person {\n  name: string\n  email: string\n  age: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = legacyCreateColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns: LegacyColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', { header: 'Name' }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('email', { header: 'Email' }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', { header: 'Age' }),\n  columnHelper.display({ id: 'actions', header: 'Actions' }),\n]\n\nfunction MyTable({ data }: { data: Person[] }) {\n  const [sorting, setSorting] = useState<SortingState>([])\n  const [columnFilters, setColumnFilters] = useState<ColumnFiltersState>([])\n  const [pagination, setPagination] = useState<PaginationState>({\n    pageIndex: 0,\n    pageSize: 10,\n  })\n\n  // useLegacyTable accepts the v8-style API\n  const table = useLegacyTable({\n    columns,\n    data,\n    getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n    getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n    getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n    getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n    state: { sorting, columnFilters, pagination },\n    onSortingChange: setSorting,\n    onColumnFiltersChange: setColumnFilters,\n    onPaginationChange: setPagination,\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <table>\n      <thead>\n        {table.getHeaderGroups().map((headerGroup) => (\n          <tr key={headerGroup.id}>\n            {headerGroup.headers.map((header) => (\n              <th key={header.id}>\n                {flexRender(\n                  header.column.columnDef.header,\n                  header.getContext(),\n                )}\n                {header.column.getCanFilter() ? (\n                  <Filter column={header.column} />\n                ) : null}\n              </th>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        {table.getRowModel().rows.map((row) => (\n          <tr key={row.id}>\n            {row.getAllCells().map((cell) => (\n              <td key={cell.id}>\n                {cell.column.id === 'actions' ? (\n                  <RowActions row={row} />\n                ) : (\n                  flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n                )}\n              </td>\n            ))}\n          </tr>\n        ))}\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction Filter({ column }: { column: LegacyColumn<Person> }) {\n  return (\n    <input\n      value={(column.getFilterValue() as string) ?? ''}\n      onChange={(e) => column.setFilterValue(e.target.value)}\n      placeholder=\"Filter...\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RowActions({ row }: { row: LegacyRow<Person> }) {\n  return <button onClick={() => console.log(row.original)}>Edit</button>\n}\n```\n\n## Type Helpers\n\nWhen using `useLegacyTable`, use these type helpers for proper TypeScript support:\n\n| Type                                | Description                                                     |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `LegacyColumnDef<TData>`            | Column definition type (equivalent to v8's `ColumnDef<TData>`)  |\n| `LegacyColumn<TData>`               | Column instance type                                            |\n| `LegacyRow<TData>`                  | Row instance type                                               |\n| `LegacyCell<TData>`                 | Cell instance type                                              |\n| `LegacyTable<TData>`                | Table instance type                                             |\n| `legacyCreateColumnHelper<TData>()` | Column helper with StockFeatures pre-bound; only requires TData |\n\n### Using `legacyCreateColumnHelper`\n\nUse `legacyCreateColumnHelper` instead of `createColumnHelper`. It has StockFeatures pre-bound, so you only need to specify `TData`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { legacyCreateColumnHelper } from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\nimport type { LegacyColumnDef } from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n\nconst columnHelper = legacyCreateColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns: LegacyColumnDef<Person>[] = [\n  columnHelper.accessor('name', { header: 'Name' }),\n  // ...\n]\n```\n\n## API Differences from v8\n\nWhile `useLegacyTable` aims for v8 compatibility, there are a few differences:\n\n### Row Model Functions\n\nThe `get*RowModel()` functions are imported from `@tanstack/react-table/legacy`:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  getExpandedRowModel,\n  getGroupedRowModel,\n  getFacetedRowModel,\n  getFacetedMinMaxValues,\n  getFacetedUniqueValues,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table/legacy'\n```\n\n### Sorting Function Renames\n\nNote that in v9, sorting-related APIs have been renamed. If you're using custom sorting functions in column definitions:\n\n| v8          | v9       |\n| ----------- | -------- |\n| `sortingFn` | `sortFn` |\n\nThe legacy table adapter handles this internally for built-in sorting, but if you're defining custom sorting functions, be aware of the rename.\n\n## Caveats and Limitations\n\n### Bundle Size\n\n`useLegacyTable` includes **all features** by default, similar to v8. This means:\n\n- No tree-shaking benefits\n- Bundle size is **much larger** than v8, since each feature has grown since v8 and you pay for all of them\n- The tree-shakeable v9 API exists so TanStack Table can add features over time without bloating everyone's bundles; only users who opt into a feature pay for it\n- If bundle size is a concern, prioritize migrating to the full v9 API\n\n### Deprecation\n\n`useLegacyTable` is deprecated and will be removed in a future major version. It exists solely to ease migration. Plan your migration timeline accordingly.\n\n### Full-State Subscription Only\n\n`useLegacyTable` always subscribes to the entire table state, so the component that creates the table re-renders on every state change, just like v8. The fine-grained rendering optimizations of v9 (narrow `useTable` selectors) are not available through the legacy hook.\n\n### No `createTableHook` Integration\n\n`useLegacyTable` cannot be used with `createTableHook`. If you want to create reusable table configurations, migrate to the full v9 API.\n\n## Migration Path\n\nOnce you're ready to migrate to the full v9 API:\n\n1. Replace `useLegacyTable` with `useTable`\n2. Define your `features` using `tableFeatures()`\n3. Convert `get*RowModel()` options to `rowModels`\n4. Update types from `Legacy*` to the standard v9 types\n\nSee the [main migration guide](./migrating.md) for complete instructions.\n\n## Example\n\nSee the [Basic useLegacyTable example](../examples/basic-use-legacy-table) for a working implementation.\n"}
